<.shell title="Activity list" current={:activity_list}>
  <h1>Activity list</h1>
  <p class="lead">A member's activities, one row each.</p>

  <div class="demo max-w-md">
    <h3 class="subheading">September</h3>
    <.activity_list
      id="activity-list-demo"
      rows={SampleData.attendances()}
      timezone="America/Vancouver"
      href={fn _activity -> "#" end}
      external={true}
    >
      <:detail :let={attendance}>
        {Service.Format.duration(
          div(DateTime.diff(attendance.activity.finished_at, attendance.started_at), 60)
        )}
      </:detail>
    </.activity_list>
  </div>

  <h2>When to use</h2>
  <p>
    One member's activities, on a phone or a narrow column: the year's activities on their own page, by month, and what they signed up for. The title links to the activity in D4H.
  </p>

  <h2>When not to use</h2>
  <p>
    A team admin's list to search, sort, or page through. Use a
    <a href={page_path(:table)}>table</a>
    with a <a href={page_path(:filter_bar)}>filter bar</a>, as on a member's Attendance tab.
  </p>

  <h2>How it works</h2>
  <p>
    Each row is the title, then the day, the kind, and a detail such as the time there. A team on SAR Duty Records gets no links, since a member cannot open its activities. The rows keep the order they come in. A heading over each month is the page's, from <code>MemberRecords.by_month/2</code>.
  </p>

  <h2>In the app</h2>
  <p>
    <code>&lt;.activity_list id rows timezone href external&gt;</code>, with rows of attendances that have their activity, and an optional <code>&lt;:detail :let=&#123;attendance&#125;&gt;</code>.
    <code>href</code>
    is a function from the activity to its URL, or nil for no links.
  </p>
</.shell>
